= Salience — Simple =

'''Salience''' means how much something stands out compared with other things.

A bright red object in a gray room is visually salient.

A sound can also become salient because it is important to you, such as hearing your name in a crowd.

Salience can pull [[Attention/Simple|attention]], but it is not the same thing as attention. You can ignore something that stands out, or deliberately focus on something that does not.

Something can also be salient without being the most important thing.

